Build a Mock Sensor 
- IoT sensors work the same way. Every message a sensor sends needs:
A timestamp — when it was sent
A counter — which number in the sequence it is
    = most common threat is a replay attack (hacker resends same attack since we dont know when it was sent if it doenst have a timestamp with it)

ISO 8601 = combination of human readable and uniz time stamp -> 2024-01-15T14:30:45Z (UTC = central time zone) 

A counter (or sequence number) is simply a number that increases by 1 with each message.


Counter Value- 
Expected: 42, Got: 42
✅ Message is valid
Expected: 42, Got: 41
⚠️ Duplicate/replayed message
Expected: 42, Got: 44
⚠️ Messages 42-43 are missing
Expected: 42, Got: 100
🚨 Something very wrong

Timestamps + Counters = Double Protection
Timestamps tell you when a message was created
Counters tell you which message it is in the sequence
Together, they make replay attacks much harder to execute!

